        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >SHORT DESCRIPTION: <strong>Astral Eden</strong> is a chapter-based, first-person atmospheric horror set in 2100. Play as <strong>Steven Wright</strong>, a night-shift worker who takes a lucrative captain’s post aboard the utopian spaceship <strong>Astral Eden</strong>, partnered with an AI co-pilot called <strong>Mastermind</strong>. You accept the job to secure your family’s future—knowing it will cost you 500 years apart—only to find that choices you made aboard the ship early on begin to unravel everything just two years into your tenure<br><br><strong><u>PLEASE NOTE: THIS GAME IS ABOUT 15 MINUTES IN LENGTH AND IS MADE BY SOMEONE WHO'S SLOW AND HAS A HARD TIME LEARNING. IF YOUR EXPECTING AAA QUALITY OR THE NEXT MASCOT HORROR CRAZE THEN PLEASE TAKE YOUR MONEY ELSEWHERE</u></strong><br><br>ABOUT: Astral Eden is a Chapter based first person atmospheric horror game set in the year 2100, You play as &quot;Steven Wright&quot; and one night while you work the night shift at your local Misfit-Market, a customer leaves behind a newspaper article for a job opening on a captain position on the newly opened &quot;Astral Eden&quot; a spaceship utopia designed and manned by one human captain and one AI co-pilot named &quot;Mastermind&quot;, Due to the significant pay raise allowing you to support your wife and future kid, you take the job at the cost of abandoning them for the next 500 years. 2 years into your tenure however, your decisions made on the ship have come to bite you in the ass.<br><br>Features:<br><br>A Slow Burn story made by someone who struggles to make a story and can only make ideas t-t</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >No real &quot;Mascot&quot; (If your looking for freddie mc-giggle fuck from Freddie's Pasta Palace then you got the wrong game kid)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >idk I'm nervous and scared to publish this, please just be nice valve</p>",
